            <ArticleTitle>A &quot;Stone in the Pond&quot; Approach to Contact Tracing: Responding to a Large-Scale, Nosocomial Tuberculosis Exposure in a Moderate TB-Burden Setting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1509-1511</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/ice.2017.228</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A &quot;stone in the pond&quot; strategy is a practical approach to investigating large-scale nosocomial tuberculosis (TB) exposures. Here, we describe such a risk-stratified approach to contact tracing after a TB exposure that occurred over 5 months in a pediatric inpatient ward in a country with a moderate TB burden. Infect Control Hosp Epidemiol 2017;38:1509-1511.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
